//
// Vocabulary is the SAME register tier one's chrome uses (src/i18n.js), one
// name per part: szerkezet, svájci horgonyjárat, gátkerék, horgonyvilla,
// billegő, hajszálrugó, főrugó, rugóház, kúpcsiga, lánc, kiskerék, korona,
// oszlopkerék, ébresztőszabályozó. One movement cannot have two names for a
// part. «kúpcsiga», never a bare «csiga», so the fusee is never read as a snail.
//
// Hungarian is AGGLUTINATIVE: a case ending attaches to a quoted identifier
// or a numeral with a hyphen, and it rides OUTSIDE the span —
// `<code>CLEAR_MARGIN</code>-ban`, `270°-os` — which is the orthography's own
// rule for a quoted token and what keeps the <code> gate byte-identical. The
// hidden .gloss-variants rows list the case forms the prose actually uses,
// read off this table's own text.
//
// NUMBERS AND <code> ARE NOT TRANSLATED — they are the source constants this
// page exists to quote, so 0.15 keeps its point here as in every locale.
// Emphasis the English carries as CAPITALS rides the wording, never an added
// tag. «modellezett» vs «szimulált» tracks the repo's modelled/simulated
// distinction exactly; HONESTY.hu gates it, and the noun «modell» is
// deliberately not the honesty word.
